{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Piper cue at edit cursor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Type a text, get it spoken by a local Piper neural voice and placed as an item at the edit cursor on a "Cues" track (created if missing). Meant for spoken cues sent to performers live ("Section B, in four", "Tacet"...), but works for any voice-over placeholder.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Fully offline and free: no API key, no internet. Works in any language Piper has a voice for (50+): the voice sets the language, so pick e.g. a German voice and type German text. Voice and speed are remembered between runs.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires Piper ({\f1 pip install piper-tts}) and at least one voice (.onnx + .onnx.json) from https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices. Run "Piper cue settings" once to point the script to Piper and the voices folder.\par}
}

