{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 vanderreaper\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaScripts for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaper.fm"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
REAPER
}}}
 by Andrea Valle (vanderaalle), mostly for live electronics and composition work.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install with ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import repositories\u8230 ?} and paste:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/vanderaalle/vanderreaper/raw/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Then browse the packages with {\i Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Browse packages}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Scripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "Piper%20cues/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Piper cues
}}}
 | Offline text-to-speech: type a text, get it spoken by a local neural voice (50+ languages) and placed at the edit cursor. Made for spoken cues to performers. |\par}
